\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Author of faith, eternal Word,
\par Whose Spirit breathes the active flame;
\par Faith, like its Finisher and Lord,
\par To-day as yesterday the same:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. To Thee our humble hearts aspire,
\par And ask the gift unspeakable;
\par Increase in us the kindled fire,
\par In us the work of faith fulfil.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. By faith we know Thee strong to save;
\par Save us, a present Saviour Thou!
\par Whate'er we hope, by faith we have,
\par Future and past subsisting now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To him that in Thy name believes
\par Eternal life with Thee is given;
\par Into himself he all receives,
\par Pardon, and holiness, and heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The things unknown to feeble sense,
\par Unseen by reason's glimmering ray,
\par With strong, commanding evidence
\par Their heavenly origin display.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Faith lends its realizing light,
\par The clouds disperse, the shadows fly;
\par The Invisible appears in sight,
\par And God is seen by mortal eye.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

